## Why This Is Asked
This question tests understanding of order statistics in dynamic multisets with duplicates and efficient prefix queries—skills fundamental to database indexing and ranking problems.

## Key Concepts
- **Balanced BST with per-node counts and subtree sizes** enables O(log n) operations
- **Handling duplicates via dupCount** avoids unnecessary node creation
- **getRank as a prefix-count query** is analogous to order statistics

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(key) {
    this.key = key;
    this.dup = 1;
    this.left = null;
    this.right = null;
  }

  get size() {
    return this.dup + (this.left?.size ?? 0) + (this.right?.size ?? 0);
  }
}

class Treap {
  constructor() {
    this.root = null;
  }

  insert(key) {
    this.root = this._insert(this.root, key);
  }

  _insert(node, key) {
    if (!node) return new Node(key);
    if (key === node.key) {
      node.dup++;
    } else if (key < node.key) {
      node.left = this._insert(node.left, key);
    } else {
      node.right = this._insert(node.right, key);
    }
    return node;
  }

  erase(key) {
    this.root = this._erase(this.root, key);
  }

  _erase(node, key) {
    if (!node) return null;
    if (key === node.key) {
      node.dup--;
      if (node.dup === 0) return this._merge(node.left, node.right);
    } else if (key < node.key) {
      node.left = this._erase(node.left, key);
    } else {
      node.right = this._erase(node.right, key);
    }
    return node;
  }

  _merge(left, right) {
    if (!left || !right) return left ?? right;
    // Simplified: in a real Treap, merge by priority
    return this._bstMerge(left, right);
  }

  _bstMerge(left, right) {
    if (!left) return right;
    if (!right) return left;
    const node = left;
    node.right = this._bstMerge(node.right, right);
    return node;
  }

  getRank(v) {
    return this._getRank(this.root, v);
  }

  _getRank(node, v) {
    if (!node) return 0;
    if (v < node.key) {
      return this._getRank(node.left, v);
    }
    const leftSize = node.left?.size ?? 0;
    return leftSize + node.dup + this._getRank(node.right, v);
  }
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests understanding of stack augmentation, a practical pattern for maintaining auxiliary state. It demonstrates the ability to design data structures that support efficient queries while handling edge cases like duplicates and empty states.

## Key Concepts
- Two auxiliary stacks (minStack and maxStack) track running minima and maxima in sync with the main stack
- Each push/pop operation updates all three stacks atomically, preserving O(1) time complexity
- Duplicates are handled naturally since the min/max is recalculated at each step
- Empty stack edge cases must be handled (typically by checking stack length before accessing top)

## Code Example
```javascript
class MinMaxStack {
  constructor() {
    this.stack = [];
    this.minStack = [];
    this.maxStack = [];
  }

  push(x) {
    this.stack.push(x);
    this.minStack.push(
      this.minStack.length ? Math.min(x, this.minStack[this.minStack.length - 1]) : x
    );
    this.maxStack.push(
      this.maxStack.length ? Math.max(x, this.maxStack[this.maxStack.length - 1]) : x
    );
  }

  pop() {
    if (this.stack.length === 0) return undefined;
    this.minStack.pop();
    this.maxStack.pop();
    return this.stack.pop();
  }

  top() {
    return this.stack[this.stack.length - 1];
  }

  getMin() {
    return this.minStack[this.minStack.length - 1];
  }

  getMax() {
    return this.maxStack[this.maxStack.length - 1];
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests advanced spatial indexing with dynamic updates and order statistics in 3D, relevant for large-scale simulations (NVIDIA) or online marketplaces with spatial constraints (Instacart, Amazon).

## Key Concepts
- 3D range trees and nested segment trees
- Weight compression and Fenwick trees for counts/sums
- Order statistics via binary search over weight indices
- Handling duplicates via multiplicities per weight index
- Fractional cascading for faster multi-node queries

## Code Example
